  "details": "Build ID: 1275\n\ndesktop mode\n\n## Details\n\n When the action layer is animating (e.g. VRCEmote != 0), changes to facial expressions are not reflected in the remote. This problem occurs even when \"Eye & Eyelid\" and \"Mouth & Jaw\" in the Tracking Control is set to \"Tracking.\" We've only checked this if the facial expression animation references GestureLeft and is implemented in the FX Layer above \"All Parts.\" Other animation on FX Layer is synced if the Action Layer is animating.\n\n## Step to Reproduce\n\n1. Use avatar with Action Layer animation and facial expression (e.g. avtr_e525d58f-7d95-4062-aef1-d3affde3c8e9).\n\n2. Play animation of action layer such as default dance motion.\n\n3. Change your facial expression.\n\n4. The expression you changed in step 3 will not be synced with other player, but displays correctly on local.",
